def page_document_reader() -> str:
    actions = button("Attach note", icon_name="pen", toast="Research memo attached to selected passage.") + button("Create evidence record", kind="primary", icon_name="plus", toast="Evidence-record form opened with selected passage.")
    outline = ''.join([f'<a class="list-item" href="#sec-{i}"><span class="list-content"><span class="list-title">{label}</span><span class="list-meta">p. {page}</span></span></a>' for i, (label, page) in enumerate([("Abstract",1),("Introduction",2),("Theory",4),("Methods",7),("Results",12),("Discussion",17),("References",22)], 1)])
    content = dedent(f"""
      <div class="toolbar"><button class="btn btn-sm">← Previous</button><button class="btn btn-sm">Next →</button><span class="toolbar-spacer"></span>{badge('Local permitted copy', 'success')} {badge('Parse quality 94%', 'brand')} {badge('Page anchor stable', 'info')}<button class="btn btn-sm">100%</button></div>
      <section class="document-viewer">
        <aside class="card card-lg document-outline"><div class="card-header"><div><h2 class="card-title">Document outline</h2><div class="card-subtitle">Alvarez et al. (2026)</div></div>{icon('book')}</div><div class="list">{outline}</div><div class="divider"></div><div class="tiny muted">Parser: Docling local baseline<br>Revision: sha256:4d9…b21<br>Rights: project-only use</div></aside>

        <article class="paper-page" aria-label="Mock article page">
          <div style="text-align:center;color:#526079;font:600 12px/1.4 Arial,sans-serif">JOURNAL OF CREATIVE BEHAVIOR · 2026 · VOL. 60(2)</div>
          <h1 style="font-size:30px;line-height:1.25;text-align:center;margin:2rem 0 .6rem">Human–AI Co-creation and the Dynamics of Creative Evaluation</h1>
          <p style="text-align:center;font-style:italic;color:#526079">Maya Alvarez · Jin Kim · Rohan Patel</p>
          <h2 id="sec-1">Abstract</h2><p>Generative systems increasingly participate in both the production and evaluation of ideas. We examine whether model-generated alternatives change creative performance through increased ideational variety, altered evaluative confidence, or both.</p>
          <h2 id="sec-3">Theory</h2><p>We distinguish creative production from creative evaluation and argue that human expertise changes how model output is interpreted. The same suggestion may function as a generative stimulus for novices and as a comparative benchmark for experts.</p>
          <p><mark>Participants who received model-generated alternatives produced more conceptually diverse revisions than control participants, but the effect on evaluated originality depended on prior domain expertise.</mark></p>
          <p>The interaction suggests that measured “creativity gains” may combine at least two mechanisms: expanded search through the idea space and changed confidence in evaluative judgments.</p>
          <h2 id="sec-4">Methods</h2><p>We recruited 184 participants and used a 2 × 2 mixed experimental design. Participants completed an ideation task, reviewed either model-generated or human-curated alternatives, and then revised and evaluated their work.</p>
          <h2 id="sec-5">Results</h2><p><mark>The model-alternative condition increased semantic distance among revisions (M = 0.41, SD = 0.09) relative to control (M = 0.34, SD = 0.08), t(182) = 5.58, p &lt; .001.</mark> However, expert ratings of originality showed a significant interaction with participant expertise.</p>
          <h2 id="sec-6">Discussion</h2><p>These findings qualify broad claims that generative AI directly increases creativity. The observed benefit is stronger for search diversity than for judged originality and appears contingent on expertise and evaluation procedure.</p>
        </article>

        <aside class="card card-lg document-inspector"><div class="card-header"><div><h2 class="card-title">Selected passage</h2><div class="card-subtitle">p. 13 · Results · paragraph 2</div></div>{badge('Observed', '')}</div><blockquote style="margin:0;padding:.85rem;border-left:3px solid var(--brand-500);background:var(--surface-2);font-size:var(--text-xs);line-height:1.6">The model-alternative condition increased semantic distance among revisions… However, expert ratings of originality showed a significant interaction with participant expertise.</blockquote><div class="divider"></div><dl class="key-value"><dt>Anchor</dt><dd>page:13 · bbox: 82,214,482,146</dd><dt>Element ID</dt><dd class="mono">el_8f2a1c</dd><dt>Parse revision</dt><dd class="mono">docrev_019</dd><dt>Rights</dt><dd>Inspect and derive; no source export</dd></dl><div class="divider"></div><h3 class="card-title">Candidate evidence</h3><div class="chip-row"><span class="chip">Expertise boundary</span><span class="chip">Semantic diversity</span><span class="chip">Originality measure</span></div><div class="toolbar" style="margin-top:1rem"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="evidence-matrix.html">Open evidence matrix</a><button class="btn" data-toast="Alternative extraction shown.">Compare extraction</button></div><div class="notice warning"><span>{icon('warning')}</span><div><div class="notice-title">Export restricted</div><div class="notice-text">The source passage may support derived records and citations but cannot be redistributed in a project bundle.</div></div></div></aside>
      </section>
    """)
    return shell("document-reader", "Document Reader", "Inspect permitted full text, parsed structure, tables, figures, citation contexts, and stable page-level evidence anchors.", content, actions, "Source inspection")


